    "headline": "NextEra, Brookfield plan $100 billion Kentucky data center campus",
    "summary": "NextEra Energy, Brookfield and other companies are developing a $100 billion data center ‌campus at a former uranium enrichment site ‌in Paducah, Kentucky, the companies said on Wednesday.  Soaring U.S. electricity demand ​is pushing companies to invest heavily in artificial intelligence data centers and other technologies straining an aging U.S. electric grid.  NextEra, the largest U.S. utility, would ‌deliver 2 gigawatts of ⁠natural gas-fired power and 2.6 GW of battery storage capacity to support the ⁠data center, while Brookfield would own and operate the 1.8 GW campus, the companies said.",
